From c972e296991fda04484a4b03a07ac58c24d9372e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:19:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: MGMT: Report a timed out command as
 MGMT_STATUS_TIMEOUT

When the controller stops answering, MGMT commands such as Set Powered,
Add UUID, Remove UUID or Set Device Class fail with Authentication
Failed although no authentication took place. With a Write Class of
Device timing out during Remove UUID, btmon showed "Remove UUID
(0x0011) ... Status: Authentication Failed (0x05)" and bluetoothd
logged "Failed to remove UUID: Authentication Failed (0x05)".

The synchronous command path returns -ETIMEDOUT when the controller
does not answer, and mgmt_errno_status() maps -ETIMEDOUT to
MGMT_STATUS_AUTH_FAILED. Map it to MGMT_STATUS_TIMEOUT instead,
matching mgmt_status_table[], which already maps the HCI timeout
statuses that bt_to_errno() turns into ETIMEDOUT to
MGMT_STATUS_TIMEOUT.

MGMT commands that fail with -ETIMEDOUT now complete with Timeout
(0x08) instead of Authentication Failed (0x05). Pairing results take
HCI statuses through mgmt_status_table[] and are unchanged.

Fixes: 161510ccf91c ("Bluetooth: hci_sync: Make use of hci_cmd_sync_queue set 1")
---
Tested in QEMU with BlueZ's doc/tester.config and a new mgmt-tester
case, "Set Device Class - Timeout 1", sent to BlueZ separately: its
emulated controller drops Write Class of Device. On bluetooth-next
cf357cfc025e the case gets Authentication Failed in 3 of 3 runs
without this patch and passes 3 of 3 with it. The patched kernel also
carried a one-line Read Advertising Features fix sent separately;
besides the two new cases, no mgmt-tester, l2cap-tester, smp-tester or
mesh-tester result changed.

 net/bluetooth/mgmt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index d21538634bc3..117ae7ab070b 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@ static u8 mgmt_errno_status(int err)
 	case -EBUSY:
 		return MGMT_STATUS_BUSY;
 	case -ETIMEDOUT:
-		return MGMT_STATUS_AUTH_FAILED;
+		return MGMT_STATUS_TIMEOUT;
 	case -ENOMEM:
 		return MGMT_STATUS_NO_RESOURCES;
 	case -EISCONN:

